From: GRAPS@galileo.arc.nasa.gov
Subject: Re: Swastika origin

Benjamin Eli Delfin said:

>I once read, I forget where, that the swastika was in fact of *natural*
>origin.  The article said that, based on someone's accidental findings
>in a lab, that a comet grazing the atmosphere could somehow interact
>with the monotomic hydrogen in the tropopause(?) and produce a large,
>glowing swastika

I'm puzzled by this. I don't know how someone could accidently
find this out in a lab unless it was a computer simulation?

I've not heard of this possible folklore. In 1986, a man
named Louis Frank claimed that, after careful analysis
of 3 1/2 years of  ultraviolet (atomic oxygen 1304 angstrom 
wavelength) data from the earth-satellite Dynamics
Explorer, he saw thousands of atmospheric "holes" that 
could not have been due to instrumental defects. Frank
claimed that his "holey" data was due to a large influx
of comets hitting our upper atmosphere and possibly
providing much more water than geologists thought for
Earth's early history. I've seen those images, and they 
really are just holes, not something like a swastika. 

{I never followed up his claim in the years after, 
unfortunately, so I don't know how the scientific frenzy
that Frank initiated, ended. In 1986 one of my jobs was analyzing
Pioneer Venus' ultraviolet data, and my boss and I
looked very carefully in all of the 1304 angstrom data 
we had showing Venus' full image, and we didn't see any 
"holes" in our data. We figured if there was a comet
influx hitting Earth, it should have been hitting Venus
too.}

Amara Graps
